end_repeating_outside.plain, line 2: Delete this line.

    end repeating
    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Why: To Plain, a line that starts with "end" only marks where steps end, like "end repeat". Plain says "stop repeating" to leave a repeat, and this line isn't among the steps of one.

end_repeating_outside.plain, line 5: Delete this line, or write "end repeat" instead.

    end the repeat
    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Try this:
    end repeat
Why: Plain knows only "end", "end if", "end repeat" and "end try", and it doesn't need them. It goes by how far each line is moved to the right.

end_repeating_outside.plain, line 9: Write "end repeat" or "stop repeating" instead.

